(:review
  :date "2026-09-11"
  :repository "/Users/purplelephant/projects/asex"
  :mode :readOnly
  :decision :amendBeforeImplementation
  :rankOrder :consequenceDescending
  :priority "Self-hosting and independence from foreign binaries, WASM enablement, semantic coherence and portable tooling; compatibility may be broken per the user’s latest instruction."
  :scope "Concept audit of 18 intended v5 rules, 11 ADR revisions, all nine drivers and six phase plans; recommendations only, repository plans were not edited."
  :method "Original sources distinguish measured scope from architectural principle. A doctrine statement is evidence of intent, not independent evidence for its own empirical claim. Missing support is explicitly (:evidence :none). No causal ASL benchmark was run. Static gates establish missing contracts, not runtime correctness."
  (:inputMismatch :expectedVersion 5 :actualAgentsVersion 4 :actualAgentsRules 17 :reviewedRules 18 :evidence ["AGENTS.md:2" "asl/grammar/rules.asn:1" "asl/grammar/rules.asn:53"] :note "The eighteenth rule, ssot, is reviewed from rules.asn; it is absent from AGENTS.md. Do not report the requested v5 block as present in AGENTS.md.")
  (:coverage :phaseTaskRecords [7 7 8 4 5 13] :uniqueTasks 41 :taskRecords 44 :revisions 11 :rules 18 :note "Phase441 has duplicate records for Task44108, Task44109 and Task44110. Every broad goal has planned work; gaps below identify narrower acceptance obligations, not absent entire programs.")
  (:rule :id semantics :verdict :confirm
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:14" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase436LanguageSemanticsGroundTruth.asn:22" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase436LanguageSemanticsGroundTruth.asn:66" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "Keep binding imports, rejecting unbound names and rejecting non-true test results as language/test contracts. They are necessary for meaningful verification and self-hosting. The current-runtime diagnosis is an earlier audit claim at the cited lines, not independently re-executed in this conceptual review; its exact 52.7% figure remains unverified here. Confirm the principle, not completion of Phase436.")
  (:rule :id gates :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:17" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase439EfficiencyFinalReview.asn:23" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase439EfficiencyFinalReview.asn:30" "https://arxiv.org/html/2501.12862v1" "https://arxiv.org/html/2607.22880v1"]
    :note "Keep negative controls and immutable acceptance criteria. Assertion inversion establishes reachability/failure propagation; it is not production-code mutation sensitivity. Report both, with equivalent/invalid mutants distinguished, and retain independent real-bug oracles. A baseline failure must be the intended semantic failure, not a missing command, parse error or grep label. Neither cited paper verified the plan’s 53% plateau or its 100%-coverage/4%-mutation anecdote in this review; drop those numbers unless exact tables are supplied. Mutation score is a proxy, not correctness.")
  (:rule :id foreign :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:26" ".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:15" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase438LanguageOptimizationAndPortableCore.asn:22" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase440FullAslSelfHosting.asn:56" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase440FullAslSelfHosting.asn:88" "https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/code-execution-with-mcp" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "Keep ASL-owned semantics and explicitly declared bootstrap/host boundaries as architectural choices. Pure source, self-hosting, autonomous rebuild and absence of an external runtime are different properties. Phase440 still invokes wasmtime and retains C. The no-new-ecosystem rule requires an explicit build/test/bootstrap exception for the planned C/WASI toolchain. MCP removal is an owner choice; code execution with MCP does not establish that removing MCP causes efficiency. No evidence supports purity or a CLI alone as a universal performance gain.")
  (:rule :id hiddenTests :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:43" "https://arxiv.org/html/2510.20270v1" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase441AttentionProsthesis.asn:158" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase436LanguageSemanticsGroundTruth.asn:30"]
    :note "ImpossibleBench supports protected hidden evaluation but reports a legitimate-performance cost and also recommends read-only tests. Its prompting results are model/task-dependent, including 92% to 1% on Conflicting-LiveCodeBench; the universal six-point claim and ONLY-hidden wording are unsupported. Keep hidden independent acceptance tests and prevent author modification of graders; permit read-only public regression tests and explicit author-owned development tests. Task44105’s edit/write ownership does not enforce a read ban or block shell access.")
  (:rule :id ssot :verdict :confirm
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:53" "AGENTS.md:2" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase437ClientLaunchAndCodexEfficiency.asn:233" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase437ClientLaunchAndCodexEfficiency.asn:237" ".agents/skills/asl-toolbelt/SKILL.md:15"]
    :note "Keep a canonical rule source and generated projections. Physical static comparison found 17 v4 AGENTS rules versus 18 v5 canonical rules, disproving current surface identity despite the task’s done receipt. This is direct evidence for drift prevention, not proof of the historical exact seven-copy count. Check per-client/per-tier projections against their deterministic expected rendering, rather than requiring all projected payloads to be byte-identical.")
  (:rule :id oneStep :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:37" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase441AttentionProsthesis.asn:31" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase438LanguageOptimizationAndPortableCore.asn:151" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase438LanguageOptimizationAndPortableCore.asn:246" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "Keep one authorized step per session and evidence before advancement as a control principle; no causal performance measurement supplied. Define a step as a transaction with an owned write set and closing gate: multiple independent edits inside that step may be batched. Multiple agents may each have a step. A caller-supplied exit=0 and nonempty receipt must not suffice: the runner must bind the receipt to the gate, tested content and session.")
  (:rule :id anchor :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:34" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.10039" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase441AttentionProsthesis.asn:30" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase441AttentionProsthesis.asn:190"]
    :note "The May 2026 study reports 5.6% lower odds per generated function (OR 0.944), not a fixed compliance percentage decline; it is exploratory, non-monotonic, and limited to Claude Code annotation behavior in two TypeScript projects. It does not prove re-anchoring restores compliance. Keep external working memory on principle; intervention efficacy is already a Task44106 hypothesis. Ledger commands are planned, so mandatory use needs a capability-aware fallback today.")
  (:rule :id context :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:5" "https://openreview.net/pdf?id=qBcHWGBnIb" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.19724" "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching" "https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/advanced-tool-use"]
    :note "AutoExperiment Table 8 supports 41.7 embedding retrieval versus 36.1 full context in scientific code infilling; AST retrieval is 33.3, so these numbers do not establish superiority of ASL symbol slices. Claude documentation supports cache hierarchy and discounted reads, with model-specific pricing and cache eligibility. Deferred discovery can preserve the prefix. Keep a stable base plus relevant retrieval; drop universal cross-provider price and whole-cache claims. Host tools are fixed by the session, not changed by this review.")
  (:rule :id output :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:8" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.29676" "https://openreview.net/pdf?id=zz157frmbC" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.16746v4"]
    :note "Notation Matters compares TOON/TRON against JSON across five open-weight models and four benchmarks. The 9/14-point losses and 18/27% savings are selected extrema, not uniform tool-result penalties; the paper includes a TRON gain for one model and no ASN arm. Keep typed receipts and recoverable evidence, but drop the ban on all compression. Separate reversible formatting/deduplication from lossy omission; compare end-to-end success and total cost before adopting a compact representation.")
  (:rule :id budget :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:40" "https://arxiv.org/html/2507.11538v1" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.21433v3" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase441AttentionProsthesis.asn:137" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase441AttentionProsthesis.asn:190"]
    :note "IFScale establishes model-dependent instruction-load effects, not a universal small-model decay law or a six-call threshold. Observation masking in Complexity Trap is a counterexample to the claimed exclusivity of task-boundary compaction. Keep explicit context/cost budgets as principle, make six calls provisional, and use the already planned calibration. A read-only review should run relevant static checks rather than arbitrary repository tests merely because six searches elapsed.")
  (:rule :id bounded :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:46" "https://www.trychroma.com/research/context-rot" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase441AttentionProsthesis.asn:95" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase437ClientLaunchAndCodexEfficiency.asn:188"]
    :note "Chroma supports nonuniform degradation and distractor sensitivity in an 18-model investigation, not decreasing accuracy at every increment in every model. Keep bounded relevant retrieval with continuation; a complete small file can fit the bound. Limit the aggregate batch response as well as each child result, and version continuation cursors so parallel mutations cannot mix snapshots. The planned 2000-token per-op cap is a tunable policy, not a literature-derived optimum.")
  (:rule :id grading :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:20" "https://openreview.net/forum?id=IkmD3fKBPQ" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.13076" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.10054"]
    :note "Intrinsic self-correction and self-preference research justify external evidence and independent checking, not universal failure of correction with executed feedback. A fresh session of the same model need not remove correlated bias. The persona study finds no overall factual-QA benefit across 2410 questions, not literally zero benefit for all engineering roles. Keep writer/grader separation and read-only scouting; make verification depend on reproducible evidence rather than role labels.")
  (:rule :id tools :verdict :confirm
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:2" ".agents/skills/asl-toolbelt/SKILL.md:72" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase436LanguageSemanticsGroundTruth.asn:98" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase436LanguageSemanticsGroundTruth.asn:130" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase438LanguageOptimizationAndPortableCore.asn:119"]
    :note "The rule correctly prioritizes available structural RPC and explicitly permits host search/edit fallbacks. In this review batched reads returned requested slices, while ASN outline returned no symbols for the ADR; status alone was not treated as semantic coverage. Current unimplemented-operation descriptions are declared baseline status, not freshly executed mutation probes. Retain capability truth and per-item error inspection; the speed advantage of this particular CLI remains unmeasured here.")
  (:rule :id concepts :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:23" ".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:9" "asl/bench/published_claims.asn:6" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase439EfficiencyFinalReview.asn:85" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "Keep empirical claims auditable, but distinguish normative design decisions from experimental hypotheses and measured facts. Requiring a baseline-failing efficacy gate before every principle is admitted would exclude git and oneStep and conflicts with planned future ledger commands. Historical audit text repeats its own conclusions; the exact old SNR/sovereignty/homeostasis failure claims have no raw audit dataset linked here. Keep explicit principles without fabricated measurements; require source, scope and uncertainty for numbers.")
  (:rule :id names :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:11" "TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md:12" "TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md:14" "TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md:17" "asl/bench/asn_tokens.lock:21" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "Keep conventional meaningful composite names and a consistent case convention. The -50/-44% examples are local documentation assertions, not a pinned, reproduced tokenizer experiment in this review; tiktoken is not installed. The lock records context-dependent alias costs, which supports rejecting a universal alias-saving rule. Neither two examples nor cl100k establish an optimum across tokenizers, code contexts or ASL task success. Drop guaranteed percentages pending Task43806/Task43903 reproduction.")
  (:rule :id edge :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:49" "https://openreview.net/forum?id=IkmD3fKBPQ" "https://arxiv.org/html/2510.20270v1" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase441AttentionProsthesis.asn:254" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "Keep explicit uncertainty, containment and escalation on principle. No measurement establishes that this five-stage ordering is optimal, or that every absent plan step is hallucination. If an action is unauthorized or cannot safely be contained, escalate immediately; do not require attempting mutation first. Planned stage/flush and escalate operations cannot be required before they exist. External checks support the mechanism, not the entire philosophical rationale.")
  (:rule :id git :verdict :confirm
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:29" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "Keep intended-only diffs, base/log verification and user-authorized commits as change-control principles. No empirical why is stated and no quantitative performance evidence is required to honor user authority. The co-author field is host policy, not a language-efficiency claim. Permission to break compatibility does not authorize unrelated deletion or publishing.")
  (:rule :id parallel :verdict :amend
    :evidence ["asl/grammar/rules.asn:32" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase438LanguageOptimizationAndPortableCore.asn:246" "AGENTS.md:115" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "Keep concurrent independent reads; no measurement establishes four/six agents or globally single-threaded writes as optimal. Use conflict-free owned partitions with one writer per partition and serialized conflicting commits, consistent with Task43808. The lean-supervisor exception is appropriate when delegation overhead dominates. User authorization permits breaking compatibility, not unnecessary parallel overhead.")
  (:revision :n 11 :verdict :amend
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:32" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase439EfficiencyFinalReview.asn:23" "https://arxiv.org/html/2501.12862v1"]
    :note "Keep falsifiable gates and real fault detection. Replace the substitution of assertion inversion for mutation testing; add semantic negative controls to existing gates rather than another gate framework. A useful failure on baseline is necessary but insufficient: the same gate can later pass a stub if it checks only an output label.")
  (:revision :n 2 :verdict :amend
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:23" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.16827" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase440FullAslSelfHosting.asn:150" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "S-expressions simplify parsing and AST manipulation; merely writing an S-expression does not guarantee balanced syntax, well-formed strings, valid types or AST/source isomorphism. Specify parse/print laws and check them. Low-resource-language literature supports caution, not a measured ASL penalty; the Racket/Python numbers in the plan were not traced to an exact original table. Keep the language choice on engineering principle and assess ASL directly.")
  (:revision :n 8 :verdict :amend
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:29" "https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/code-execution-with-mcp" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase437ClientLaunchAndCodexEfficiency.asn:29"]
    :note "A single CLI is a coherent product boundary and complete MCP removal is already an owner decision; do not re-propose it. The cited efficiency pattern works with MCP and does not justify protocol removal empirically. Shell-only interoperability is narrower than all-host portability, and AGENTS.md/SKILL.md portability depends on host recognition. State these as supported-client contracts.")
  (:revision :n 1 :verdict :amend
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:22" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.06007" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.15516" ".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:12"]
    :note "Stable reusable context and precision are well-supported levers, but density is not universally third-order. If a cached prefix costs 0.1 per token, reducing its length by 30% saves 30% of that prefix’s cached bill, equivalent to 3% of the original uncached bill; those are different denominators. The stated 88% lacks a workload model. Optimize total cost per correct task, including writes, misses, outputs, tool calls and latency; CAPC is promising limited evidence, not a universal result.")
  (:revision :n 9 :verdict :amend
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:30" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase437ClientLaunchAndCodexEfficiency.asn:74" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase437ClientLaunchAndCodexEfficiency.asn:140" ".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:47"]
    :note "Keep removal of duplicate and irrelevant injection; existing receipts document launch improvements but not end-to-end causal accuracy. The 2500-token budget is an engineering target, while ADR consequences still say under 5000; specify payload versus whole session and model tokenizer. Preserve necessary semantics and mandatory capabilities even when a tier is compact; do not equate a byte limit with a token limit.")
  (:revision :n 10 :verdict :confirm
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:31" "https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/advanced-tool-use" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase438LanguageOptimizationAndPortableCore.asn:119" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase441AttentionProsthesis.asn:95"]
    :note "Retain progressive disclosure and batch orchestration. The vendor reports tool-discovery savings and model-specific selection gains, supporting the direction, though not ASL batch superiority or the claim that this is the strongest paradigm in every workload. Search before loading and keep source references recoverable; existing tasks already serve this goal.")
  (:revision :n 6 :verdict :amend
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:27" "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.10054" ".asl/mem/tasks/Phase441AttentionProsthesis.asn:315"]
    :note "Drop unsupported teleological persona performance claims and retain mechanical ownership and independent grading. Exactly two roles is not an experimentally established optimum; scoped scouts and domain profiles can coexist without persona prose. Six domain profiles in Task44110 should earn their complexity through distinct permissions and measured work, as that task’s failure mode already requires.")
  (:revision :n 3 :verdict :amend
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:24" "asl/bench/asn_tokens.lock:21" "TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md:12"]
    :note "Retiring the universal one-to-two-token basis is justified: the cl100k lock itself has contextual abbreviations that cost more or equal tokens. Keep semantic names, but neither ban useful domain aliases nor advertise CamelCase as the sole possible optimization. Bare identifier wins do not imply whole-program or cross-model gains.")
  (:revision :n 4 :verdict :amend
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:25" "asl/bench/token_frames.lock:2" "asl/bench/token_frames.lock:4" "asl/bench/token_frames.lock:9" "asl/bench/asn_tokens.lock:4" "asl/bench/published_claims.asn:7" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "Correcting the 72% claim is justified. The available lock contains 51 JSON versus 18 positional tokens and 0.6471 saving under cl100k, but the generating fixture/script is not supplied by that receipt, so it proves neither a global ceiling nor the indented-JSON comparison nor real-data parity. ASN strings still need escaping. Preserve types, ordering where meaningful, duplicate-key policy, numeric domains and escaping in round-trip tests; no format is inherently zero-escaping.")
  (:revision :n 7 :verdict :confirm
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:28" ".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:28" "AGENTS.md:243" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "Suspend SNR>=0.75 as an unsupported quantitative invariant. A BPE count alone would still not measure semantic signal: numerator, denominator, labels and relationship to task outcomes need definition. Keep relevance as a qualitative principle; do not resurrect an arbitrary ratio merely because a gate can count tokens.")
  (:revision :n 5 :verdict :amend
    :evidence [".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:26" ".asl/mem/decisions/Adr0081LanguageGroundTruthAndSovereignPortabilityProgram.asn:26" "TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md:24" (:evidence :none)]
    :note "The reframing correctly abandons an unmeasured speed claim, but a universal comment ban is not established as an effective stale-comment defense. Keep rationale near canonical contracts and decisions; require consistency checks for generated or duplicated explanation. Drop C1 as an unconditional cognitive/performance invariant unless the team deliberately chooses it as a style policy; its benefit is presently principle-only.")
